fix(adb): cancelling a phone connect stops leaving the pane blank with no way out

`device-connect.svelte.ts` holds the pane's listing while it works, so a `null` view state renders NOTHING: no file
list, no sentence, no button. Four paths set exactly that. Both Cancel closures (the one on `connecting` and the one on
`waiting_for_device`) and the backend's own `cancelled` answer left it, and `onMount` had already skipped
`loadDirectory` while `path-sync` answers `none` at an unchanged path, so the effect would not re-dial either. The only
escape was switching volumes. The untyped-failure branch released the hold instead and said the listing's error pane
would take over, but only the success path calls `onConnected`, so nothing ever restarted the listing: the same empty
pane, minus the message.

Every way a dial can end now leaves something to read and, where a second try could work, something to press.

- A cancel renders `refused` with the new `adb.connect.cancelled` ("You stopped opening your phone.") and a Try again.
  Matter-of-fact, no scolding: "a cancel says nothing" is about not lecturing someone for what they did on purpose, not
  about leaving them staring at an empty pane.
- An untyped failure renders `adb.connect.transport` with a Try again. Its own text is untranslated diagnostics and
  still goes only to the log.
- A device row whose path names no serial renders `adb.connect.deviceGone` with no button, since nothing a person
  presses fixes a malformed row. It used to release the hold and show nothing, the same bug one branch over.

❗ Releasing the hold is deliberately NOT the escape hatch: `list_directory` on an `adb://` path re-dials the phone
through the backend's own `adb-navigation:<serial>` id, so letting the listing run would redial the thing the user just
called off.

Four cells, plus the existing cancel cell rewritten from "says nothing" to "leaves a way back in". Translations for the
new key in all ten locales, register matched to the `adb.connect.*` siblings and the verb taken from each locale's
existing `search.coverage.walk.cancelled` rather than its Cancel-button label.
